ou wash your hands and you should try  not to touch your face as much as  possible how do I know if I'm infected  the only way to know for sure if you  have kovat 19:00 is to take a test  because many of the symptoms are similar  to those people experience when they  have other respiratory ailments like the  flu in kovat 19 the primary symptoms  that people have reported our fever dry  cough and fatigue and then to a lesser  extent things like aches congestion a  sore throat or diarrhea some people who  catch the disease don't have any  symptoms at all they're asymptomatic  around 4 &amp; 5 people who get it will  recover from the disease without any  special treatment or having to go to the  hospital what can I do if I'm infected  because this virus is a novel one in  humans no one has any immunity the first  time they catch it even if someone  doesn't show any symptoms they still  grow infected and can infect others we  don't yet have any specific vaccines to  prevent kovat 19 and we don't have any  medications to treat it so at this point  if you are infected  there's no way to interrupt the course  of the disease the best thing to do if  you're infected is to talk with your  local medical authorities and follow  their advice if you aren't in a  high-risk group for the disease the  chances are very good you'll return to  full health within a couple of weeks  if I've had it once can I catch it again  in the future because this is a new  virus we still don't know much about how  the immune system will react to  subsequent infections with kovat 19  doctors assume that catching it will  give you some kind of immunity but a big  question is exactly how long that  immunity will last our immunity levels  to related coronaviruses like some that  caused common colds are not permanent  and we don't really know why the  question of immunity is a question that  really only time will answer a news team  at the Austrian public broadcaster ORF  will go into voluntary isolation 